.SH NAME
id \- print user and group \s-1ID\s+1s and names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B id
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Id\^
writes a message on the standard output giving the user
and group \s-1ID\s+1s and the corresponding names of the
invoking process.
If the effective and real \s-1ID\s+1s do not match, both
are printed.
.SH SEE ALSO
logname(1),
getuid(2),
getgid(2).
